# Dependencies and build output
node_modules
dist
dev-dist
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Logs and OS cruft
*.log
.DS_Store

# Editor and tooling state
.idea/
.vscode/
.playwright-mcp

# Local configuration. `.env.example` is the tracked template and stays in.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Self-hosted runtime data: the SQLite database and anything else the server
# writes. docker-compose.yml mounts ./data into the container, so this keeps a
# host's own health log out of the repository.
data/

# Food illustration pack — a separate release artifact, not part of the repo.
# Fetch it with scripts/fetch-food-pack.mjs
food-pack/

# Agent workspace: local MCP settings and planning specs. These are working
# notes, not published documentation — they are written against the hosted
# service this project was converted from, so they describe infrastructure and a
# commercial surface that no longer exist and would only mislead a reader.
# `docs/architecture.md` is the tracked description of how the code works now.
.kiro/

# The old marketing site. SnapGut is self-hosted software, so `/` serves the app
# and there is no landing page in this repository any more. These sources are
# kept on disk only to seed a separate `snapgut-website` repo — nothing in the
# build, the server, or the tests reads them. `marketing/assets/` holds the
# illustrations and the Open Graph card that moved out of `public/` with them.
# The substance of the privacy and terms pages lives on as docs/privacy.md and
# docs/terms.md.
marketing/
